pocket-ui @VERSION@ for the Retroid Pocket Mini V2: SD card image
================================================================

pocket-ui is a game launcher with its own libretro frontend. This card starts it next to Android:
Android and its partitions stay as they are, and nothing is flashed to the device.

The system underneath is based on ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@ (https://rocknix.org). pocket-ui is not made or
endorsed by the ROCKNIX team.


Install
-------

1. Write pocket-ui-@VERSION@-rp-mini-v2.img.xz to a microSD card with balenaEtcher or Raspberry Pi
   Imager. Both read the .xz file directly. Everything on the card is erased. 8 GB or more.
2. Put the card into the switched-off device.
3. Once: hold Volume Down and press Power. Retroid's fastboot menu opens, and its bottom line reads
   "Boot mode: Android". Pick "Switch boot mode" with the volume keys and press Power until it reads
   "Boot mode: Loader", then pick "Start".
   Volume Up + Power does not start the loader on current Retroid firmware; use the boot mode.
4. The first start takes a few minutes and restarts once by itself while the card's storage is set up.
   Then pocket-ui's first-start setup opens: look, Wi-Fi, extras.

The boot mode is stored: from now on, switching on starts pocket-ui while the card is in.

Back to Android: hold Volume Down and press Power, pick "Switch boot mode" until the bottom line reads
"Boot mode: Android", then "Start". The card can stay in.

If the screen stays black with "Boot mode: Loader", the device's loader partition holds no u-boot
(an Android update can replace it). Switch back to Android as above and see the pocket-ui
documentation (INSTALL-DUAL-BOOT.md, "Only if the loader holds no u-boot").

This card contains no BIOS files and no games. Add only games and BIOS files you own.
Remote access (SSH), file sharing and Syncthing are off. When you turn on Remote access or file
sharing in pocket-ui's Settings, it makes a password for this device and shows it on the screen.
(EmulationStation, ROCKNIX's menu, can also turn SSH on; it then uses ROCKNIX's standard root password
"rocknix" until you change it there.)
Do not install ROCKNIX updates on this card: they replace the system but not the kernel in
boot/pocket/, and the two must match.


What is on the card
-------------------

FAT partition "ROCKNIX" (readable on any computer):
  KERNEL, KERNEL.md5         ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@, unchanged (ROCKNIX-SM8250.aarch64-@ROCKNIX_TAG@.img.gz)
  SYSTEM, SYSTEM.md5         ROCKNIX @ROCKNIX_TAG@'s system, repacked without the files listed under
                             "Changes" below; everything else in it is unchanged
  EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI      GRUB, started by Retroid's u-boot in "Boot mode: Loader"
  boot/grub/grub.cfg         no menu, starts boot/pocket/Image
  boot/pocket/Image          the Linux kernel, unpacked unchanged from KERNEL
  boot/pocket/miniv2-noufs.dtb   the Mini V2 device tree from KERNEL, with the internal storage
                             switched off, so the system never sees Android
  post-flash.sh              boot hook: starts without the ROCKNIX logo
  mount-storage.sh           boot hook: puts pocket-ui's start entry in place once the storage has
                             grown, then deletes itself
  pocket-ui-info/            this file; SOURCE-OFFER.txt; pocket-ui's LICENSE and NOTICE.md;
                             licences/ (the Rust crates' licence texts and the fonts' OFL; also in
                             STORAGE as /storage/pocket-ui/licences); rocknix-licenses/ (ROCKNIX's
                             LICENSE.md and licenses folder at tag @ROCKNIX_TAG@); firmware-licences/
                             (the terms of the firmware files inside SYSTEM)

Partition "STORAGE" (grows to fill the card at the first start):
  pocket-ui/                 pocket-ui, pocket-core and pocket-splash (the boot screen) @VERSION@, the launcher
  .pocket-seed/              the start entry for pocket-ui and the boot screen's unit (moved to
                             .config/system.d at the second start)

Changes from the ROCKNIX image: the files above were added. The folder rocknix_abl/ (a replacement for
Retroid's bootloader, not used here) was removed. Removed from SYSTEM:
  - the Kickstart relocation tables (kick*.RTB) of Amiberry's WHDLoad booter, loose and inside its
    boot-data.zip (the rest of that archive is unchanged). They come from SKick
    (aminet.net, util/boot/skick346.lha), whose licence allows passing them on only inside that unchanged
    archive. Amiga games run with the standard emulator (PUAE) as before; for WHDLoad games in Amiberry,
    copy the .RTB files from that archive to /storage/.config/amiberry/whdboot/save-data/Kickstarts.
  - firmware for the AYN Thor and the Mangmi Pocket Max (no licence stated; the Mini V2 does not use it).
  - the DOOM shareware game data (usr/share/idtech/doom.tar.gz), so the card holds no games; its
    shareware terms also ask for the complete, unchanged shareware package.
  - ROCKNIX's ABL bootloader and its flash scripts (usr/share/bootloader/rocknix_abl; no licence stated, and
    this card never flashes a bootloader).
The partition table and KERNEL are unchanged. ROCKNIX's own interface, EmulationStation, stays on the card
and takes over if pocket-ui cannot start.


Licences
--------

This image may be shared free of charge, for non-commercial use only. Do not sell it, and do not
bundle it with hardware you sell. Reasons: ROCKNIX includes components licensed for non-commercial use
only (for example the libretro cores snes9x, genesis_plus_gx, picodrive and fbneo), and its artwork is
licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

ROCKNIX (KERNEL, SYSTEM)
  Copyright ROCKNIX (https://github.com/ROCKNIX). ROCKNIX is a fork of JELOS
  (https://github.com/JustEnoughLinuxOS/distribution); credit to the JELOS team.
  The ROCKNIX team's own software and scripts: GNU GPL version 2. Every bundled component keeps its own
  licence: see pocket-ui-info/rocknix-licenses/ (ROCKNIX's LICENSE.md and licenses folder) and each
  package's PKG_LICENSE in ROCKNIX's source.
  ROCKNIX branding and images (logos, splash artwork, EmulationStation themes inside SYSTEM):
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ . They are included unchanged
  inside SYSTEM; this image does not use them as its own branding.
  The GBA BIOS file inside SYSTEM (usr/config/nanoboyadvance/bios/gba_bios.bin) is not Nintendo's: it is
  the open-source replacement BIOS by Normmatt and the VBA-M team from ReGBA
  (https://github.com/Nebuleon/ReGBA, bios/), GNU GPL version 2 or later. ROCKNIX ships it unchanged.

Firmware inside SYSTEM (usr/lib/kernel-overlays/base/lib/firmware): Qualcomm GPU, DSP, video, Wi-Fi and
  Bluetooth firmware and a Realtek USB network firmware from linux-firmware 20260309, and the wireless
  regulatory database from wireless-regdb 2026.05.30, all unchanged. They may be passed on under the terms
  in pocket-ui-info/firmware-licences/ (README.txt there lists every file and its terms).

Linux kernel (boot/pocket/Image, the kernel in KERNEL): GNU GPL version 2.
  The device tree is ROCKNIX's, with two nodes set to "disabled".

GRUB (EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI): GNU GPL version 3 or later.
  Debian package @GRUB_VERSION@, made with grub-mkimage.

pocket-ui and pocket-core
  GNU GPL version 2 or later (pocket-ui-info/LICENSE).
  Source: @POCKET_UI_SOURCE@.
  Third-party credits (fonts, Rust crates and other parts, each under its own licence) are in
  NOTICE.md: pocket-ui-info/NOTICE.md on this card, and in the repository. The licence texts of the Rust crates
  and of the fonts (SIL Open Font License) are in pocket-ui-info/licences/.


Source code
